; BASIC Program
;
; #HTML(Velnor's Lair by Derek Brewster, published by Neptune Computing
; in 1983. It is the first of his two "Myths and Legends of Caraland"
; games; <a href="https://spectrumcomputing.co.uk/entry/7157"
; rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">Spectrum Computing</a> also notes
; the Quicksilva reissue and the sequel, Kentilla.)
; .
; #HTML(The whole game is a ROM-loaded BASIC program. The tape header
; names it "VELNOR", sets autorun at line 4860, and gives a program length of
; #N($93D2,$04,$04) and a data length of #N($A112,$04,$04). There is no
; custom tape loader.)
; .
; #HTML(Line 4860 is <code>POKE D,F: GO TO A</code> with the saved
; variables <code>D=23728</code> (#SKOOLKID$5CB0(NMIADD)), <code>F=4</code>
; and <code>A=1</code>, so it writes #N($04) to NMIADD and starts at line 5.
; Line 4870 (<code>PRINT USR TU</code>) is not the autorun path.)
; .
; #HTML(Line 6035 POKEs a #N($10)-byte routine at #R$FF58 that writes
; attribute #N($38) across the screen; line 6330 calls it with
; <code>RANDOMIZE USR 65368</code>. That code is not on the tape and is not
; present in this snapshot.)
